{#
  Thin band of community names, used in place of a "where we work" section.

  Replaces a heading + eyebrow + paragraph that said the same thing in prose:
  the names ARE the message, so they carry it directly. Renders from
  src/_data/serviceArea.json, the same list the homepage marquee loops, so a
  community is named once in the project and appears identically everywhere.

  Not a marquee and not interactive: nothing here animates, so there is no
  motion to pause and no control to provide. That is the point of the strip.

  `aria-label` names the band for a screen reader, which otherwise meets a
  bare list of 28 place names with no indication of what they are.
#}
<section class="locations locations--strip" aria-label="Communities we work in">
  <ul class="location-strip">
    {%- for place in serviceArea.communities %}
    <li>{{ place }}</li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
